0","idp_filedate":1792386614000,"nhcTitle":"Off the East Coast of the United States","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area is located along a  frontal boundary a few hundred miles off the southeast coast of the  United States. This low is likely to move slowly and erratically  over the next couple of days, and it could gradually acquire  subtropical characteristics if it remains over the Gulf Stream. A  subtropical cyclone could form during the middle to latter portions  of the week when the system begins to move northeastward away from  the eastern United States. Environmental conditions are expected to  become unfavorable for development by the weekend. Regardless of  the system's status, high winds, coastal flooding, and dangerous  surf are expected along portions of the U.S. East Coast during the  next few days. Please consult statements and warnings from local  National Weather Service offices and the Weather Prediction Center  for more information, along with High Seas Forecasts and Storm  Warnings issued by the National Weather Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.02055651271871,6.294640532589432],[-92.83742964164311,6.305702029876423],[-92.65711267998294,6.318143380732606],[-92.47971563297948,6.331994194709443],[-92.30534850587404,6.347284081358398],[-92.13412130390786,6.364042650230934],[-91.96614403232223,6.382299510878515],[-91.80152669635844,6.402084272852603],[-91.64037930125774,6.423426545704661],[-91.48281185226139,6.446355938986154],[-91.32893435461075,6.470902062248543],[-91.17885681354701,6.497094525043293],[-91.03268923431148,6.524962936921865],[-90.89054162214543,6.554536907435726],[-90.75252398229014,6.585846046136336],[-90.6187463199869,6.618919962575159],[-90.48931864047698,6.653788266303658],[-90.36435094900165,6.690480566873297],[-90.243953250802